{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-05_q1-27pressreleaseexhibit991.htm, sha256 0958a0845623b39f7b601fe2d50e15d49a2b50801e64ca654f0b4565686d590d.\nEX-99.1 2 q1-27pressreleaseexhibit991.htm EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1\nOpenText Reports First Quarter Fiscal Year 2027 Financial Results Core Revenues growth of 2% Y/Y, and Core Cloud Revenues growth of 11% Y/Y Delivers Net Income Margin of 13%, Robust Adjusted EBITDA Margin of 35.8%\nFiscal 2027 First Quarter Highlights (in millions)(1)\nTotal Revenues Cloud Revenues Profitability EPS Cash Flows\nNet Income A-EBITDA GAAP Non-GAAP Operating Free Cash Flow\n$1,237 $505 $155 $442 $0.64 $1.05 $172 $139\n-4.0% Y/Y +4.3% Y/Y 12.6% margin 35.8% margin +10.3% Y/Y \u2014% Y/Y +16.6% Y/Y +36.8% Y/Y\nWaterloo, ON, November 5, 2026 - Open Text Corporation (NASDAQ: OTEX), (TSX: OTEX), today announced its financial results for the first quarter ended September 30, 2026.\n\u201cOur first quarter reflects the strength of our core portfolio and the value we deliver for clients,\u201d said Ayman Antoun, OpenText CEO. \u201cAs clients move to AI, they need trusted context and connected data for outcomes they can rely on. With Aviator AI agents infused across our core portfolio and a go-to-market model built around our clients' success, we are supporting them at every step of their AI journey.\u201d\nAyman Antoun, OpenText Chief Executive Officer\n\u201cOpenText delivered strong performance in the first quarter of Fiscal 2027, supported by continued financial and operational discipline,\u201d said Steve Rai, OpenText EVP, CFO. \u201cFollowing the quarter, we completed a $1.0 billion debt refinancing and paid down $300 million in debt through a successfully completed tender offer, providing the Company with greater financial flexibility. The durability of our operating model enables us to execute our capital allocation priorities through the remainder of Fiscal 2027.\u201d\nSteve Rai, OpenText Executive Vice President, Chief Financial Officer\nFirst Quarter Financial Highlights Y/Y \u2022Total revenues: $1.237 billion, -4.0% Y/Y, -1.7% Y/Y in constant currency excluding divestitures \u2022Core Revenues(2): $864 million, +2.4% Y/Y, +2.7% Y/Y in constant currency \u2022Core Cloud Revenues(2): $339 million, +11.2% Y/Y, +11.7% Y/Y in constant currency \u2022Annual recurring revenues (ARR): $1.040 billion \u2022Cloud revenues: $505 million, +4.3% Y/Y, 23 consecutive quarters of cloud organic growth \u2022Cash flows: Operating $172 million and free cash flow(3) $139 million \u2022Net income: GAAP $155 million, +5.9% Y/Y, Non-GAAP(3) $254 million, -4.5% Y/Y \u2022Adjusted EBITDA(3) of $442 million, margin of 35.8% \u2022Diluted earnings per share (EPS): GAAP $0.64, Non-GAAP(3) $1.05 \u2022Repurchased $23 million of common shares for cancellation\n"}
