{"page": 3, "text": "Dividend As part of the quarterly, non-cumulative cash dividend program, the Board declared on November 3, 2026, a cash dividend of $0.280 per common share. The record date for this dividend is December 4, 2026 and the payment date is December 18, 2026. OpenText believes strongly in returning value to its shareholders. Any future declarations of dividends and the establishment of future record and payment dates are all subject to the final determination and discretion of the Board of Directors. Quarterly Business Highlights \u2022In October, OpenText completed a $1.0 billion senior secured notes offering, with proceeds used to retire its outstanding 2027 notes. OpenText further reduced its debt by $300 million as part of a successfully completed tender offer of a portion of its outstanding 2028 notes. Including debt repaid in October 2026, the Company has reduced debt by approximately $949 million over the past twelve months. Our net leverage ratio is 2.55x as of September 30, 2026. \u2022OpenText, Cohere partnered to combine trusted data with agentic AI \u2022OpenText had a number of key client wins in the quarter representing a diverse set of industries across the globe. \u25e6Key wins in the Americas included: Workplace Safety & Insurance Board (WSIB) \u25e6Key wins in EMEA and the rest of the world included: Commerz Real AG, Gruppo CAP, Insurance Australia Group (IAG), and Sumitomo Electric Wiring Systems Inc. 2\nSummary of Quarterly Results\nQ1 FY\u201927 Q4 FY\u201926 Q1 FY\u201926 % Change (Q1 FY\u201927 vs Q4 FY\u201926) % Change (Q1 FY\u201927 vs Q1 FY\u201926)\nRevenues (millions) $ 1,236.6 $ 1,349.0 $ 1,288.1 (8.3) % (4.0) %\nGAAP-based gross margin 73.2 % 75.0 % 72.8 % (180) bps 40 bps\nNon-GAAP-based gross margin (1) 76.9 % 78.3 % 76.5 % (140) bps 40 bps\nGAAP-based EPS, diluted $ 0.64 $ 0.64 $ 0.58 \u2014 % 10.3 %\nNon-GAAP-based EPS, diluted (1) $ 1.05 $ 1.23 $ 1.05 (14.6) % \u2014 %\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "(1)Please see Note 2 \u201cUse of Non-GAAP Financial Measures\u201d to the condensed consolidated financial statements below. Conference Call Information OpenText posted an investor presentation on its Investor Relations website and invites the public to listen to the earnings conference call webcast on Thursday, November 5, 2026 at 8:00 a.m. ET (5:00 p.m. PT) from the Investor Relations section of the Company\u2019s website at https://investors.opentext.com. To join the webcast instantly, use this webcast link. A webcast replay will be available shortly following completion of the live call. Please see below note (2) for a reconciliation of U.S. GAAP-based financial measures used in this press release to Non-GAAP-based financial measures. Save the Date for OpenText Investor Day: February 10, 2027 OpenText intends to host an Investor Day on Wednesday February 10, 2027 in Toronto, Canada. The event will also be available by audio webcast for investors who wish to attend virtually. At the Investor Day, OpenText CEO Ayman Antoun and members of the Executive Leadership Team will discuss the outcome of the previously announced Enterprise Assessment. This includes a discussion of the Company\u2019s strategic priorities, growth initiatives, and financial framework.\nFor more information, please contact: Greg Secord Vice President, Global Head of Investor Relations Open Text Corporation (416) 956 0380 (Canada) / (415) 963 0825 (U.S.) investors@opentext.com\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 OpenText. All Rights Reserved. Trademarks owned by OpenText. One or more patents may cover this product(s). For more information, please visit https://www.opentext.com/patents. About OpenText OpenText\u2122 is a global leader in data management for enterprise AI, helping organizations protect, govern, and activate their data with confidence. Our technologies turn data into information with context to form the knowledge base for enterprise AI. Learn more at www.opentext.com. 3\n"}
